DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("(e^(x))^2+1*(e^(x))+4");
$fun_1 = Formula("cos(((sin(x))/10))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("(4, 6) U (4, 6) U (4, 6)");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("((-infinity, 17]) U (4, 6) U (-infinity, 17] U (-infinity, 17] - ((-infinity, infinity) - ((((4, 6)) U (-infinity, 17]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ((-infinity, 17] U ((-infinity, 17]) U ((-infinity, 17] U (4, 6))))))");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("(4, 6) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (4, 6)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 17])");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{-7, 1, 3} - ((-infinity, infinity) - (({-7, 1, 3}))) U {-3, -1, 2, 3, 5, 6}");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-3, -1, 2, 3, 5, 6} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-3, -1, 2, 3, 5, 6}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-7, 1, 3})");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`2*9+2`]? [_____]{Real(20.)}
---

[`12+15+5+16/5`] is equal to [_____]{Real(35.2)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-3, -1, 2, 3, 5, 6\}`]
- [`B = \{-7, 1, 3\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cap ((B)) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cap A \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 4 < x < 6\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \leq 17\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`(B) \cup A \cup B \cup B \cap (((A) \cup B) \cap (B \cup (B) \cup (B \cup A))) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cap A \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 8, 8, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -2, -4, 5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 9, 3, -10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<8, 8, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, 3, -10>") x Compute("<8, 8, 0>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-2, -4, 5>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<8, 8, 0>") . Compute("<-2, -4, 5>")}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-2, -4, 5>") . Compute("<9, 3, -10>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -3, -10, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -3, -6, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 2, -3, -6 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, -6, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, -6, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-3, -6, 0>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, -10, 0>") x Compute("<2, -3, -6>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, -10, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, -10, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(8) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>8)}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>7)}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>2)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>9)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
